  "conclusion": "The central Motion effect replicates almost exactly across two independent training seeds: RC-COJA improves trained h2 by 57.39/57.60 px and unseen h3 by 39.08/41.56 px, while the h1 cost is 3.01/3.30 px. Correct-history benefit also improves at h2 and h3 in both seeds. Standard PushT effects change sign (+2.00pp and -1.33pp); the two-seed hierarchical mean is +0.33pp with a [-4.0,+4.5]pp 95% interval. Thus the large long-horizon hidden-dynamics gain and small h1 tradeoff are reproducible, while no RC-specific standard-retention effect is identified."
